1. ECLIPSE – MAVEN PROJECT
---------------------------
Import Maven project:
Eclipse
→ File
→ Import
→ Maven
→ Existing Maven Projects
→ Select project folder
→ Select pom.xml
→ Finish

Alternative:
File → Import → Git → Projects from Git → Clone URI

After importing:
Right-click project → Maven → Update Project
(or Alt+F5)

Open:
pom.xml


2. MAVEN BASIC COMMANDS
-----------------------
Check Maven + Java:
mvn -v

Check Java:
java --version

Validate POM:
mvn validate

Clean old build:
mvn clean

Compile:
mvn compile

Run tests:
mvn test

Create JAR/WAR:
mvn package

MOST IMPORTANT:
mvn clean package

Build with debug information:
mvn clean package -X

Skip test execution:
mvn package -DskipTests

Force dependency update:
mvn -U clean package

Show dependency tree:
mvn dependency:tree

Analyze dependencies:
mvn dependency:analyze

Install artifact to local .m2:
mvn install

Deploy artifact:
mvn deploy


3. MAVEN BUILD FLOW
-------------------
pom.xml
   ↓
mvn validate
   ↓
mvn compile
   ↓
mvn test
   ↓
mvn package
   ↓
target/
   ↓
.jar or .war


4. IMPORTANT POM ITEMS
----------------------
groupId       → project/organization identifier
artifactId    → project name
version       → project version
packaging     → jar / war
dependencies  → libraries required by project
plugins       → Maven build tools
finalName     → output JAR/WAR filename

Example:
<packaging>war</packaging>
<finalName>OnlineShoppingApp</finalName>

Output:
target/OnlineShoppingApp.war


